---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import Img from '../components/Img.astro';
import { A } from '../lib/assets';
import { BUSINESS, YEARS_IN_BUSINESS } from '../lib/site';

const description =
  `Building in the Conejo Valley since ${BUSINESS.founded}. CPF Custom Concrete and Masonry is an independent consulting and contracting company serving Newbury Park, Thousand Oaks and Westlake Village under California contractor license #878989.`;
---

<Layout title="About" description={description}>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About"
    title={`Building in the Conejo Valley since ${BUSINESS.founded}`}
    intro={`${YEARS_IN_BUSINESS} years of foundations, stamped concrete, natural stone, block walls and brick — from large-scale renovations to smaller residential jobs.`}
    asset={A.stoneEntry}
    displayW={1024}
  />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 prose-cpf">
    <p>
      CPF Custom Concrete and Masonry is an independent consulting and contracting
      company specializing in foundations, stamped concrete, natural stone, block
      walls and brick products. Clients enjoy the peace of mind that comes with a
      guaranteed completion date and full insurance coverage. Project expertise
      ranges from large-scale renovations to smaller residential jobs, with
      tenacious attention to detail and pride of accomplishment on every one.
    </p>

    <h2>In the Conejo Valley since {BUSINESS.founded}</h2>
    <p>
      CPF has been building here for <strong>{YEARS_IN_BUSINESS} years</strong>.
      That covers several housing booms, a couple of recessions, and a great many
      contractors who came and went in between — which is most of what a homeowner
      is really asking when they ask how long you have been doing this.
    </p>
    <p>
      It also means the work is checkable. The retaining walls in Dos Vientos, the
      ballfields at Triunfo YMCA and Viewpoint School, the driveways and outdoor
      kitchens across Newbury Park and Thousand Oaks — they are all still standing,
      and most of them are a short drive away.
    </p>
    <p>
      This website is new. The business is not. If you want to confirm that before
      you call, <strong>California contractor license #{BUSINESS.license}</strong>
      is a matter of public record and takes about thirty seconds to check on the
      <a
        href="https://www.cslb.ca.gov/onlineservices/checklicenseII/checklicense.aspx"
        rel="noopener"
        target="_blank">CSLB license lookup</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>What we actually do</h2>
    <p>
      Most of the work is residential hardscape across Newbury Park, Thousand Oaks,
      Westlake Village, Calabasas and Camarillo — driveways, patios, retaining
      walls, outdoor kitchens and fireplaces. Alongside that, CPF has delivered two
      community and institutional ballfield projects: the Triunfo YMCA baseball
      fields, and Robertson Family Field at Viewpoint School in Calabasas.
    </p>
    <p>
      Those two matter more than their size suggests. Institutional clients award
      work on scheduling and insurance as much as on craft, and they do not hand a
      live school campus to a contractor who might overrun. It is the same promise
      a homeowner is buying: the job gets finished, on the date agreed.
    </p>

    <h2>Two things worth knowing before you call</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Guaranteed completion date.</strong> Agreed at quoting, not hoped
        for afterwards. A contractor who turns up when he said he would is the
        thing most people are actually worried about.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Full insurance coverage.</strong> On every job, residential and
        commercial.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where we work</h2>
    <p>
      {BUSINESS.serviceArea.slice(0, 5).join(', ')} and the wider Conejo Valley.
      If you are just outside that, call and ask — it depends on the job.
    </p>
  </article>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 pb-16 sm:px-6">
    <div class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
      {
        [
          { asset: A.dosVientosWall, caption: 'Retaining walls, Dos Vientos, Newbury Park' },
          { asset: A.stampedDriveway, caption: 'Stamped concrete driveways' },
          { asset: A.brickFireplaceMantel, caption: 'Outdoor fireplaces and kitchens' },
        ].map((item, i) => (
          <figure>
            <Img
              asset={item.asset}
              displayW={500}
              sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 33vw"
              label={`about strip ${i}`}
              imgClass="aspect-[3/2] w-full object-cover"
            />
            <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">{item.caption}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Layout>
